"""Writes docs/longform/VISUAL-EDITING-RESEARCH.md from measured data (tables) plus findings text. Every number in the findings comes from a table row or a stored observation in notes_p3b.md."""
from docs_common import *
G = list(A[0]["groups_sampled"].keys())
L = []
n_done = len(A); n_plan = sum(PLANNED.values())
L += ["# Visual editing research (Phase 3)", "",
      f"Status: **{n_done} of {n_plan} planned reference videos analysed** (2 Celebrity News videos blocked by YouTube's bot check, see 'Incomplete'). Generated by `output/longform-research/doc_visual.py` from `docs/longform/research/phase3/aggregate.json`; per-video evidence is in `docs/longform/research/phase3/VIDEO-RECORDS.md`.", "",
      "Nothing in this document is a universal rule. Each channel group has 2-6 videos, several groups come from a single reference channel, and the percentages are estimates with stated error. Confidence is rated per finding: High = enough coverage, clear observation and manual verification; Medium = useful but limited sample / partial coverage / classification uncertainty; Low = weak or single-source.", "",
      "## 1. What was measured and how (method beside every number)", "",
      "| Measure | Method | Error / limit |", "|---|---|---|",
      "| Category share, **sampled** (S) | One frame every 15 s per video, shown as a 240-px tile with its timestamp; each tile labelled by eye (this session's model) with one code (footage V, news N, interview I, host H, photo P, historical still R, archival film/clip A, screen S, map M, tactical diagram Q, chart G, illustration D, whiteboard W, motion graphic O, text card T, decorative F, document X, AI-generated Z, stock K, black B). A '+' marks a text overlay. | Exact only at the sampled instants. Dense re-labelling of three 180 s windows (3 s step) found the largest class 5-20 points high and classes of 5-15% missed entirely on fast-cut videos (`val/*_dense_labels.json`). Treat every S figure as +-5 to +-12 points. |",
      "| Category share, **segment-weighted estimate** (W) | Video split at detected shot boundaries; each segment's time is divided between the sampled frames inside it; segments with no sample inherit the nearest sample (reported as 'inherited'). | An estimate of screen time, not a measurement. Depends on the sampled labels and on the boundary detector. |",
      "| Shot rhythm | Two detectors. (1) hard cuts from per-frame scene score (misses dissolves); (2) dissolve-aware detector: mean difference between frames 0.75 s apart at 4 fps, local maxima above 0.08, at least 1.5 s apart. | Validated on one 120 s window of one video (Pacific NW coast): about 21 changes counted by eye, detector 19, about 17 matched. Treat shots/min as +-15%. Not meaningful for whiteboard/animation videos (continuous drawing) or long pans. |",
      "| Real vs constructed | Real captured = V,N,I,H,K,P,R,A,S,X (footage, photographs, archive, genuine screen recordings and documents). Constructed = M,G,Q,D,W,O,T,F,Z (maps, charts, tactical diagrams, illustration, whiteboard, motion graphics, text cards, decorative, AI-generated). | A map built from real satellite imagery is still counted as constructed here (it is an edited graphic). Game capture is counted as real footage. |",
      "| Provenance (real vs stock vs commissioned) | Not determinable from frames. Only stated when a credit/watermark is visible. | Low confidence by construction. |", ""]
L += ["## 2. Coverage per channel", "", coverage_table(), "",
      "Coverage limits: the analysis cap is 2100 s per video. Long videos were therefore sampled over part of their length only (see the per-video 'analysed / total' in the records). Two Court & Spotlight videos were analysed from 300 s clips saved in an earlier phase because YouTube blocked re-download (`jZpq6BCud7s` 47% of the video, `-p_TBe0Re_s` 7% of an 73-minute documentary): their results are **low coverage**.", "",
      "Channel diversity of the references (matters for generalising): Hidden Past = 5 videos from one channel (RealLifeLore); AI Tested = 5 from one channel (AI Search); Rival Lines = 5 from one channel (Football Made Simple); Court & Spotlight = 3 SunnyV2 + 1 Frontline + 1 Spanish documentary channel; Celebrity News = 2 analysed (2 channels) plus the SunnyV2 Corden video that also fits; Space = 6 videos from 6 channels; Psychology = 5 videos from 5 channels. A single-channel group shows **that channel's style**, not the genre.", ""]
L += ["## 3. Category mix per channel (sampled share; range across videos in brackets)", "",
      "| Channel | " + " | ".join(G) + " |", "|---|" + "---|" * len(G)]
for c in CH:
    rs = by(c)
    L.append(f"| {CHNAME[c]} ({len(rs)}) | " + " | ".join(f"{100*wavg(rs, lambda r: r['groups_sampled'][g]):.0f}% ({rng([r['groups_sampled'][g] for r in rs], pct=True)})" for g in G) + " |")
L += ["", "Segment-weighted estimate (W) of the same groups, pooled per channel (each video weighted by its analysed length):", "",
      "| Channel | " + " | ".join(G) + " |", "|---|" + "---|" * len(G)]
for c in CH:
    rs = by(c)
    L.append(f"| {CHNAME[c]} | " + " | ".join(f"{100*wavg(rs, lambda r: r['groups_segment_weighted'][g]):.0f}%" for g in G) + " |")
L += ["", "Method for both tables: see section 1. The range in brackets is the minimum-maximum over the videos of that channel, which shows how far one video can sit from the channel average.", ""]
L += ["## 4. Real versus constructed, graphic-only stretches, human subject, overlays (sampled, per video)", "",
      "| Channel | Video (analysed %) | Real captured | Constructed | Longest all-constructed stretch (interval) | Host/interview frames | Frames with text overlay |", "|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|"]
for c in CH:
    for r in by(c):
        ra = run_at(r, "longest_constructed_run_at"); iv = f"{r['longest_constructed_run_s']} s" + (f" ({tc(ra[0])}-{tc(ra[1])})" if ra and ra[2] else "")
        L.append(f"| {CHNAME[c]} | {link(r)} ({r['coverage_pct']}%) | {100*r['real_media_share_sampled']:.0f}% | {100*r['constructed_share_sampled']:.0f}% | {iv} | {100*r['human_subject_share_sampled']:.0f}% | {100*r['overlay_share_sampled']:.0f}% |")
L += ["", "Intervals are the sampled run (each sample stands for 15 s). 'Host/interview' counts H and I frames only. In the AI Search videos a host or interviewee is at most 1% of sampled frames; in the RealLifeLore videos it is 0-1% except where public-appearance footage is used (Russia 30%, Canada 12%, Saudi Arabia 11%).", ""]
L += ["## 5. Shot rhythm per channel (dissolve-aware detector; hard-cut detector in the records)", "",
      "| Channel | Shots/min (range over videos) | Median shot length s (range) | Share of shots < 3 s | Share > 10 s |", "|---|---|---|---|---|"]
for c in CH:
    rs = [r for r in by(c) if r.get("shots2")]
    L.append(f"| {CHNAME[c]} | {rng([r['shots2']['per_min'] for r in rs], 1)} | {rng([r['shots2']['median_gap_s'] for r in rs], 1)} | {rng([r['shots2']['share_gaps_lt_3s'] for r in rs], pct=True)} | {rng([r['shots2']['share_gaps_gt_10s'] for r in rs], pct=True)} |")
L += ["", "Read with caution: the two whiteboard videos and the Mars 4K panorama video are continuous-motion formats whose 'shots' are not cuts. Median shot length of the cut-based videos falls between about 3 and 6 s in every channel; the exceptions are Mars 4K (31 s median, long panoramas), one Rival Lines video (9.0 s, How Chelsea's Tactics Beat United) and the two whiteboard videos, whose 'boundaries' are drawing steps rather than cuts.", ""]
L += ["## 6. Visual change: how much of the time the picture is nearly unchanged", "",
      "Method: per second, the median over four samples of the mean absolute difference between two frames 0.75 s apart (64x36 RGB, scale 0-1). 'Static' = below 0.01. This detects held pictures (static graphics, paused screens, title cards, dark scenes); it does not judge whether a held picture is meaningful. Camera pans and zooms on stills register as change. Validated only by spot inspection.", "",
      "| Channel | Static share of time (range over videos) | Longest static stretch s (range) | Median change score (range) |", "|---|---|---|---|"]
for c in CH:
    rs = [r for r in by(c) if r.get("motion")]
    L.append(f"| {CHNAME[c]} | {rng([r['motion']['static_share'] for r in rs], pct=True)} | {rng([r['motion']['longest_static_s'] for r in rs])} | {rng([r['motion']['median_change'] for r in rs], 3)} |")
L += ["", "The two longest static stretches are 137 s (AI Search, Cybersecurity chaos video, a page held on screen) and 103 s (History of the Universe, What Is Beyond The Edge?); everything else is under 60 s. Nothing here says a 40-second still is wrong: in the screen-recording channel it is a document being read.", ""]
open(os.path.join(HERE, "_visual_head.md"), "w", encoding="utf8").write("\n".join(L))
print(len(L), "lines")
